urce":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"c668545f1897cc30c0639d27caa1c97a797ab9091ddc27fb215133cb54db8516","quote":"We currently have approximately 5,000 software, drone services and land surveys paying corporate clients using our medical records software, SCADA & HMI software, video surveillance software, call center software and safety and compliance management software, field service management software and other services.","context":"Operations Overview","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":448,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"fc3f84d8e60059ce9c573b316896f22f1d6c215ab7e865bc23cf07cd0e57773c","quote":"Our Drone as a Service business model launched in early 2025 is currently growing by acquisitions primarily of land survey and engineering companies in which we are in the process of integrating our drones into the land surveying, scanning and inspection services and other workflows. We have also acquired a window washing company, in which we are in the process of integrating drone technology.","context":"We currently have approximately 5,000 software, drone services and land surveys paying corporate clients using our medical records software, SCADA & HMI software, video surveillance software, call center software and safety and compliance management software, field service management software and other services.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":449,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"eaa16bc2e02cdbe6199285129c15e05d357c746185c1ded6ef7046f81b0ec476","quote":"In addition, we have signed several pilot program agreements with customers across industries currently at various stages of execution to evaluate our drone technology incorporating our drone enterprise software. These pilot programs include farms in Ireland where drone applications being tested include irrigation and crop yield management, scanning and spraying the farmland, counting animals and performing scanning for security and maintenance of farm assets and buildings. In addition, we are at various stages of execution of indoor drone technology pilot programs that include an auto manufacturing company and an auto parts manufacturing company using our indoor inventory management drone. Further we have various outdoor security, traffic and crowd management, or maintenance pilot programs in progress with a multinational energy distribution center, a public horse racing course and golf course companies.","context":"Our Drone as a Service business model launched in early 2025 is currently growing by acquisitions primarily of land survey and engineering companies in which we are in the process of integrating our drones into the land surveying, scanning and inspection services and other workflows. We have also acquired a window washing company, in which we are in the process of integrating drone technology.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":450,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"22e410511880495c4b5677b081b5b61c205f7faaf6d6d11306b46e965a882d34","quote":"We generate income from our software business and services and do not anticipate any changes to the use of existing software products under our current business operated through NOW Solutions, WorkAware, PacePlus, SystemView, ZigVoice, WorkAware, TillerStack, PSPortals Interactive Systems, interlinkONE, ZooOffice and DeskFlex while we pursue our drone business. We have not made any royalty payments on our software products to date. In addition, we have not made any royalty payments on our drones, including to Epazz in respect of software used in our drones.","context":"In addition, we have signed several pilot program agreements with customers across industries currently at various stages of execution to evaluate our drone technology incorporating our drone enterprise software. These pilot programs include farms in Ireland where drone applications being tested include irrigation and crop yield management, scanning and spraying the farmland, counting animals and performing scanning for security and maintenance of farm assets and buildings. In addition, we are at various stages of execution of indoor drone technology pilot programs that include an auto manufacturing company and an auto parts manufacturing company using our indoor inventory management drone. Further we have various outdoor security, traffic and crowd management, or maintenance pilot programs in progress with a multinational energy distribution center, a public horse racing course and golf course companies.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":451,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"54686ca9cbd92a3528c67d04383364146966b96d3c275278b824d8e80077992e","quote":"We currently conduct our software business in the United States of America, Canada, Ireland, United Kingdom, United Arab Emirates, Taiwan and Germany. We currently are testing our drone technology in United Arab Emirates, the US, Ireland and soon we will start testing in Turkey.","context":"We generate income from our software business and services and do not anticipate any changes to the use of existing software products under our current business operated through NOW Solutions, WorkAware, PacePlus, SystemView, ZigVoice, WorkAware, TillerStack, PSPortals Interactive Systems, interlinkONE, ZooOffice and DeskFlex while we pursue our drone business. We have not made any royalty payments on our software products to date. In addition, we have not made any royalty payments on our drones, including to Epazz in respect of software used in our drones.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":452,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"bbade969391689a46e677a513c63336c9153236743584ccbe6cd0c9e193b1bc5","quote":"The Company has two revenue streams starting January 1, 2025, from our enterprise software and Drone as a Service business. Below is a table showing the revenue breakdown for our software companies by product type and geographical location for the years ended December 31, 2024 and 2025. There were no revenues from drones prior to 2025.","context":"We currently conduct our software business in the United States of America, Canada, Ireland, United Kingdom, United Arab Emirates, Taiwan and Germany. We currently are testing our drone technology in United Arab Emirates, the US, Ireland and soon we will start testing in Turkey.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":453,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"f46d0c95992b4491c441d056fa7bb2ebaa7507b2cd1cc4f970a6cad49f9df34a","quote":"| | Year EndedDecember 31, 2025 | | Year EndedDecember 31, 2024 Total Enterprise Software as a Service (SaaS) Revenue | $ | 2,806,988 | $ | 1,963,605 Total Drone as a Service (DaaS )Revenue - | $ | 10,105,734 | $ | Nil","context":"The Company has two revenue streams starting January 1, 2025, from our enterprise software and Drone as a Service business. Below is a table showing the revenue breakdown for our software companies by product type and geographical location for the years ended December 31, 2024 and 2025. There were no revenues from drones prior to 2025.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":454,"table":" |  | Year EndedDecember 31, 2025 |  | Year EndedDecember 31, 2024\nTotal Enterprise Software as a Service (SaaS) Revenue | $ | 2,806,988 | $ | 1,963,605\nTotal Drone as a Service (DaaS )Revenue - | $ | 10,105,734 | $ | Nil","attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"ac0d59a2b4a407ddbd17dc61df5baf645e1b341b54fc19e3d8b2f0e4f0572e4b","quote":"We signed a management service agreement with Epazz to support the development of our products. Under the agreement, we receive the benefits of various services, including a software development team, office space, project management and hosting services. Epazz is paid 30% above cost (amended from 20%).","context":"| | Year EndedDecember 31, 2025 | | Year EndedDecember 31, 2024 Total Enterprise Software as a Service (SaaS) Revenue | $ | 2,806,988 | $ | 1,963,605 Total Drone as a Service (DaaS )Revenue - | $ | 10,105,734 | $ | Nil","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":455,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a