 of Ecker (the \"Ecker Securities\") held by Ameritek, which is the sole member of Ecker.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":468,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"094ef6c586bb7b2a02ca7d5e9cb55993c0a98e5e1177916971206d4f48156a17","quote":"•5,000 Super Voting Shares with a stated value of USD$30.00,","context":"In consideration of the purchase of the Ecker Securities, ZenaTech issued to Ameritek the following shares:","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":469,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"f9bfae34791f417f137b0f06708a8789a74e249222970b7ed7349f1bc71a8614","quote":"•750,000 Preferred Shares with a stated value of USD$3.00 per Share.","context":"•1,000,000 Common Shares, and","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":471,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"bbb40559fb82e1f1748ccd34694ad24a35d31a8ba3b9c126f03f6cd0825e9615","quote":"Ecker is located at 55 E. Jackson Blvd, Suite 1005, Chicago, Illinois and is the software developer for warehouse software products. It is a benefit to ZenaDrone for its IQ drone series. Ecker is a parent holding company of Interactive Systems, Inc., interlinkONE, Inc, and ESM Software, Inc., three software technology companies.","context":"•750,000 Preferred Shares with a stated value of USD$3.00 per Share.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":472,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"d807a02822394e899bbced6104026cf116f35c1cc7d444352eb555f8aafab569","quote":"The Company has received an independent valuation of the business of Ecker, which was prepared by the Valuator. The effective date of the valuation is September 30, 2024 and is based on Ecker as an on-going concern which assumes Ecker has the financial resources to continue operating into the foreseeable future. All traditional approaches to value were considered by the Valuator and specific methods and calculations were weighted to reflect Ecker's value. Ecker was appraised using the fair market value as the standard of value assuming no discount for a lack of control (DLOC) and no adjustment for lack of marketability (DLOM). Because the balance sheet of Ecker might not represent the business, this valuation only values the enterprise value. The enterprise value is the invested capital value (debt and equity) of the business.","context":"Ecker is located at 55 E. Jackson Blvd, Suite 1005, Chicago, Illinois and is the software developer for warehouse software products. It is a benefit to ZenaDrone for its IQ drone series. Ecker is a parent holding company of Interactive Systems, Inc., interlinkONE, Inc, and ESM Software, Inc., three software technology companies.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":473,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"fe7fa6561b87f7956f70707b7b999961adaff7915d8baeb4092da23be91eaab8","quote":"The Fair Market Value (enterprise value) of Ecker is estimated at $4,144,906 USD. After any balance sheet adjustments, the adjusted value is $592,313 USD and after subtraction of term debt, if any, the equity value is $590,000 USD. Equity value subtracts interest-bearing term debt and the working capital surplus or shortage, if any, from the enterprise value. A 100.00% interest of the Company's equity equals $4,140,000 USD. The Valuator's conclusion is subject to the Report's Limiting Conditions and the note in the conclusion section.","context":"The Company has received an independent valuation of the business of Ecker, which was prepared by the Valuator. The effective date of the valuation is September 30, 2024 and is based on Ecker as an on-going concern which assumes Ecker has the financial resources to continue operating into the foreseeable future. All traditional approaches to value were considered by the Valuator and specific methods and calculations were weighted to reflect Ecker's value. Ecker was appraised using the fair market value as the standard of value assuming no discount for a lack of control (DLOC) and no adjustment for lack of marketability (DLOM). Because the balance sheet of Ecker might not represent the business, this valuation only values the enterprise value. The enterprise value is the invested capital value (debt and equity) of the business.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":474,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"ed6a72016c00dd429e01e95052f9284b9d83db9834d68c67b498ec1842895ced","quote":"The Fair Market Value (FMV) is defined as the value an asset or liability would exchange hands given a willing buyer and seller negotiate an \"arms-length\" transaction with neither party under duress and with the parties having access to all pertinent information.","context":"- 32 -","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":476,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"99a7883eba2c