forts during the period, including customer field demonstrations and the planning of ZenaDrone pilot programs for fiscal 2026. The Company’s defense‑oriented product portfolio is intended to address emerging requirements in counter‑drone, maritime interception, and autonomous intelligence, surveillance, and reconnaissance (ISR) applications.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":591,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001376474-26-000319","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-29","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001997403","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1997403/000137647426000319/zt_20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e.bin","sha256":"295395c6ca709d99c538e0f784a5448fe4c384536ae04b0309c9fca7f0ab606e"}},{"id":"e6629e2cb6b167645574b4bcb6adca9005992051a2eab1000ce7e3f60eeda98b","quote":"(xiii)Advancement of the ZenaDrone Product Family. The Company continued the development and commercialization of its ZenaDrone product family during the period, including the ZenaDrone 1000 for agricultural and defense applications, the IQ Nano indoor drone for GPS‑denied environments, the IQ Square outdoor surveying drone, and the ZenaDrone 2000 maritime interceptor platform. Following the closing of the Epazz APA described above, the Company also integrated the PIN Technology, ZD1000 Design Generation 4, ZD1000 Spraying Module, IQ Octo Drone, IQ Aqua, and Spraying Trailer Platform technology assets into its drone product roadmap.","context":"(xii)Record Annual 2025 Revenue. For the year ended December 31, 2025, the Company reported total revenue of CAD $12,912,722, representing growth of approximately 556% compared to fiscal year 2024. The DaaS segment contributed approximately 78% of the Company’s 2025 annual revenue.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":592,"table":null,"attribution":"is